# A station sitting on the TNC ports, doing nothing until a client arrives.
#
#   app/ardop-spine --null 600 --host 8515 --script test/app/idle.script
#
# Then, in another terminal:
#
#   telnet localhost 8515        MYCALL, VERSION, STATE, ARQBW all work
#   telnet localhost 8515        a second one is refused with a reason
#
# Watch the "[a] TNC client attached; it owns the link" line: from that moment
# @stats reports credit=0 with "TNC client owns the link", and it goes back to
# 4096 the instant the client disconnects. That is the takeover rule
# (analysis/14 Decision 4) with nothing else to it -- the TCP disconnect is the
# release, so there is no claim to leak and no state to get stuck in.

MYCALL N0AAA
ARQBW 2000MAX
LISTEN TRUE

@echo waiting for a TNC client; Ctrl-C to stop

@stats
@wait secs=5
@stats
@wait secs=5
@stats
@wait secs=10
@stats
@wait secs=30
@stats
